 Next slices should wire these planners deeper into concrete hot paths after local JDK 25 Gradle validation: entity tracker candidate selection, chunk interest fanout, compression scheduling, and per-region survival hotspot measurements.
+
+
+## R22 / alpha14 - Wild-scale kernel first
+
+This release moves the roadmap from many independent optimisation helpers to a single wild-survival scale kernel. Important optimisations now happen before micro-tuning:
+
+1. Reserve visible-latency CPU for the main thread, plugins, Netty, GC and OS.
+2. Spend remaining cores only on read-only prepare, fanout de-duplication, chunk intent planning, entity candidate preselection and ordered-commit preparation.
+3. Use region hotspot accounting so spawn/town clusters share duplicate read-only plans instead of repeating them per player.
+4. Use explicit thread-affinity/plugin logic translation so multi-threading cannot mutate Bukkit state or reorder plugin callbacks.
+5. Keep hard gameplay rules as invariants: no packet drop, no FIFO skip, no entity tick skip, no off-thread Bukkit mutation, no event reorder.
+
+Next roadmap step after alpha14 is fine-grained optimisation inside these kernels: packet shape hashing quality, chunk intent cache compaction, region hotspot eviction, visibility band precomputation and command/API polish.
